14:- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input with extra properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L86)).
15:- For a root-level invalid property, the rejection names the property path without adding a leading dot ([validated by: reports root property paths without a leading dot](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L113)).
20:- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
23:- Reusing the same schema object from a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` compiles it only once ([validated by: compiles a function-valued schema once when the same schema object is reused](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L70)).
27:- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).

